{"site_id": "417b5d77-c70a-40ad-adad-7f92ef1a0544", "site_name": "Roma Dönemi Agora Harabeleri", "table": "unified_sites", "column": "site_type", "current_value": null, "proposed_value": null, "reason": "field-unresolved", "note": "The sources describe the monument as an agora (Eşiz Mersin: 'the basilica with 5 naves built during the Byzantine period on the city agora (assembly area) in the Roman period'), but the canonical type list has no agora type, and none of the sources calls it a forum or any other canonical type, so no value can be sourced.", "phase3": false, "finding_test_id": "WD3/site_type", "evidence": []}
{"site_id": "417b5d77-c70a-40ad-adad-7f92ef1a0544", "site_name": "Roma Dönemi Agora Harabeleri", "table": "unified_sites", "column": "source_url", "current_value": null, "proposed_value": null, "reason": "field-unresolved", "note": "No page was found that is about a Roman-period agora at this point: the pages that exist (Wikipedia, Eşiz Mersin, the Italian mission at Sapienza) treat it as part of the wider Elaiussa Sebaste city, and the earlier pass's Agora of Smyrna results belong to a different site in İzmir. The field stays empty.", "phase3": false, "finding_test_id": "WD3/source_url", "evidence": []}
